Manual steps remaining:

# 1Password
- Open seahorse
- Create a "login" keyring with no password
- Sign in to 1Password
- Lock, unlock, enter 2FA code

# Helium
- Install 1Password browser extension
- Log into Tailscale admin console
- Log into iCloud (needed for rclone; see iCloud section)

# Tailscale
- Connect
- Run `tailscale set --accept-dns=true --accept-routes`
- Fix exit node: check admin console ("cannot relay traffic")

# iCloud
- Run `rclone config` and follow prompts to add a remote named `icloud`
- When tokens expire (monthly), log into icloud.com when prompted — gatherd-prompt-icloud extracts cookies and updates rclone automatically
- [Details](https://forum.rclone.org/t/icloud-connect-not-working-http-error-400/52019/44)

# Claude
- Desktop: log in via the app
- Code: run `claude` in a terminal

# Zoom
- Log in
- Try sharing a window — confirm screen sharing works under Sway/wlroots

# JetBrains Toolbox
- Log in to your JetBrains account by clicking the tray icon

# Timeshift
- Open Timeshift, confirm BTRFS is selected, click Finish

# Verify
- Screen lock: let screen time out, then wiggle/tap — should see lock screen
{% if has_resume %}
- Screen lock: close lid, reopen — should see lock screen
{% endif %}
- LocalSend: check alias is system hostname, not a random phrase
- On low-RAM machines: Helium → Settings → Performance — Memory Saver should be Maximum
- Systray (fast-path): after first login, 1Password, Tailscale, and arch-update tray icons appear without logging out
- Systray (slow-path): LocalSend and JetBrains Toolbox tray icons appear as soon as slow install finishes, without logging out
- JetBrains Toolbox: first launch goes straight to main screen, no user agreement dialog
- Systray (idempotency): run `gatherd-systray <app> [args...]` again — no duplicate tray icons appear
- Helium: first launch opens directly to browser, no setup tab
- NFS automount: access `~/.autofs-mounts/code` — should mount from ap-juicer transparently
- iCloud: run `rclone lsd icloud:` — should list top-level folders without error
- iCloud re-auth: log out of icloud.com in Helium, log back in — `rclone lsd icloud:` should work again without manual steps
- Captive portal: join a portal network, confirm Helium opens automatically and portal login works
- Power management: run `tlp-stat | head -30` — confirm "Status: enabled" and correct power source
- Power management: run `sudo powertop --time=5` — Tunables tab should be mostly "Good"
- Power management: on battery, run `upower -i $(upower -e | grep BAT)` — check energy-rate in watts
{% if has_thinkpad_hardware %}
- Power management (ThinkPad): run `tlp-stat -b | grep -i thresh` — confirm 75/80 thresholds
- ThinkPad fan control: run `cat /proc/acpi/ibm/fan` — should show current speed level and RPM
- ThinkPad fan control: run `systemctl status thinkfan` — should be active
- TrackPoint scroll: in any scrollable window, hold middle button and push TrackPoint — should scroll
- ThinkVantage button (T60): press blue ThinkVantage button — should open a terminal
{% endif %}
{% if has_ir_receiver %}
- IR receiver: run `ls /dev/lirc* /sys/class/rc/rc* 2>/dev/null` — should show at least one device
- IR receiver: run `ir-keytable` — confirm device listed with a keymap loaded
- IR receiver: run `ir-keytable -t -s rc0` and press remote buttons — should show scancode + keycode per press
{% endif %}
